 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 516556,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the total if 41% of the total is 342. If necessary, round to two decimal places.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The formula relating the total (base), the percent in decimal form, and the part (amount) is</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"part = percent \\times total\"></span>.</p>\n<p>342 is 41% of the total.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"342 = 0.41 \\times total\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{342}}{{0.41}} = \\frac{{\\cancel{{0.41}} \\times total}}{{\\cancel{{0.41}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The total is approximately 834.15 (rounded to two decimal places).</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "834.15 (rounded to two decimal places)"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
